diff --git a/src/Changelog.md b/src/Changelog.md
index 5747756..1d89b25 100644
--- a/src/Changelog.md
+++ b/src/Changelog.md
@@ -4,6 +4,93 @@ All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.
 The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](http://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/)
 and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).
 
+## [1.2.0-mt14] - 2026-11-19 (answers version 1.2.64)
+- Kick sidechain defaults to off. Hold Accent, tap and release Transpose Up to toggle it in any mode. Green means on, red means off. The choice is saved across restarts. The two-arrow mode chord still takes priority.
+- USB SysEx F0 7D 64 0E 00/01 F7 sets the same preference. Diagnostics append two bytes for sidechain state and clock source.
+
+## [1.2.0-mt13] - 2026-11-19 (answers version 1.2.63)
+### Fixed (found by recording both instruments through an audio interface, and by the third outside review)
+- Ducking under the DRUM's kick stepped the gain at an audio block boundary, a tick about 25 dB under the note. The dry voice now has its own gain stage that glides over 2.9 ms
+- A transpose button acts when it is let go, so pressing the two mode buttons one after the other never leaves the synth a semitone off. The further octave at either end of the range now needs a hold of 0.3 s
+
+## [1.2.0-mt12] - 2026-11-19 (answers version 1.2.62)
+### Added (from the second outside review)
+- Filter envelope with a decay: 8/120 ms to 50 % in techno, 13/150 ms to 55 % in organic (stock held the filter open while the note was held)
+- The dry voice ducks under the DRUM's kick (notes 30-37 on channel 10): -3 dB and 115 ms back in techno, -1.5 dB and 85 ms in organic
+- Accents per step: hold Accent while stopped and press a step. Plain / accented velocity 100/119 techno, 94/109 organic
+- Third mode, "organic east": the organic voice with harmonic minor keys. Organic itself now has the pentatonic keys
+- New start patterns for techno and organic
+
+### Changed
+- Voice, echo and reverb numbers of both voices; built-in hat sends less into the effect
+
+### Fixed
+- A key held across a mode switch released the wrong note and left the old one hanging
+- The first of the two mode buttons no longer transposes on the way; a held pair switches once
+- Waiting for the master's clock is dropped on Stop and on our own Play
+- Echo and reverb levels glide to their new values on a mode switch
+- The mode flash no longer depends on the millisecond counter not wrapping
+
+## [1.2.0-mt11] - 2026-11-19 (answers version 1.2.61)
+### Added
+- Second synth mode, "organic": D# harmonic minor keys, softer and darker voice, shorter echo, more reverb, its own start patterns. Both transpose buttons together switch modes; the keys flash blue (techno) or amber (organic). Stored in EEPROM. Sysex f0 7d 64 0d <mode> f7
+
+### Fixed (from an outside review)
+- Note pitch was cut down to whole hertz (stock): up to 17 cents flat in the bass
+- A write one element past the LED array at every power up, and out of range indexing for MIDI channels 11-16 (stock)
+- A MIDI Start or Continue no longer lets the internal clock play a step before the master's first clock; a position after a clock pause honours the tempo knob multiplier; Continue without a position resumes on the next clock instead of acting like the Play button
+- MIDI thru off: a device after the DUO got every clock twice
+- The cutoff calculation no longer runs with the audio interrupt held off
+
+## [1.2.0-mt10] - 2026-11-19 (answers version 1.2.60)
+### Changed
+- Sawtooth and pulse oscillators with band-limited steps (src/synth_blep). The stock ones alias: thin whistles above 6 kHz, heard most with detune and an open filter. Same pitch, level and pulse width as before
+
+## [1.2.0-mt9] - 2026-11-19 (answers version 1.2.59)
+### Fixed
+- Filter cutoff tops out at 780 Hz instead of 1.8 kHz. With the cutoff knob fully open and little resonance the filter overflowed and put out loud noise (mt1-mt8)
+
+## [1.2.0-mt8] - 2026-11-19 (answers version 1.2.58)
+### Changed
+- Speaker amp: wakes with the audio muted for 30 ms and then fades the sound in; fades out before it sleeps; sleeps after 2.5 s of silence. mt7 kept it on for a minute, which stopped most clicks but let the idle hum through
+
+## [1.2.0-mt6] - 2026-11-18 (answers version 1.2.56)
+### Changed
+- Following a Dato DRUM at half speed (tempo knob fully left): after its Stop and Play the pattern continues in the half it stopped in, not always in the first
+
+## [1.2.0-mt5] - 2026-11-18 (answers version 1.2.55)
+### Changed
+- MIDI input takes up to four messages per pass, so the first note after the master's Play is not late
+- Several MIDI clocks arriving between two passes of the main loop all count (stock dropped all but one)
+
+## [1.2.0-mt4] - 2026-11-18 (answers version 1.2.54)
+### Changed
+- The speaker amp stays on until the output has been quiet for a minute (4 seconds in mt4-mt6). It used to switch off after 50 ms, and fading echo and reverb tails made it click on and off
+
+## [1.2.0-mt3] - 2026-11-18 (answers version 1.2.53)
+### Added
+- Song Position Pointer followed by Continue starts at that place in the bar, over the MIDI socket and USB. Made for the Dato DRUM duo-team build, which resumes mid-pattern
+
+## [1.2.0-mt2] - 2026-11-18 (answers version 1.2.52)
+### Changed
+- When the MIDI clock stops for a second, tempo goes back to the knob (stock stayed a follower until power off)
+- Internal clock no longer runs about 3 % slow
+- MIDI Start over USB starts from the first step, like Start on the MIDI socket
+- Pressing Play while following an external clock: comes back in on the master's bar position (after a MIDI Start), and a press just after the beat plays that step at once
+
+## [1.2.0-mt1] - 2026-11-18 (melodic techno build, answers version 1.2.51)
+### Added
+- Space effect on the delay switch: delay at a dotted eighth of the current tempo with darker, thinner repeats, plus a reverb (src/effect_space)
+- Sysex f0 7d 64 0c f7 returns audio load figures
+- Four D# minor start patterns instead of random notes
+
+### Changed
+- Keys play D# natural minor instead of the pentatonic scale
+- Detune knob: octave below, fifth below, fourth below, unison detune (the -9 and -4 semitone zones are gone)
+- Filter cutoff is exponential, 40 Hz to 1.8 kHz (was linear 30-541 Hz); resonance goes up to 3.8 (was 3.2)
+- Amp attack 5 ms (was 2 ms) to stop the click on a note from silence
+- The stock delay was set to 440 ms but the library capped it at 337 ms; it is replaced by the space effect
+
